  "question": {
    "text": "A copper rod of mass $\\mathrm{m}$ slides under gravity on two smooth parallel rails, with separation $l$ and set at an angle of $\\theta$ with the horizontal. At the bottom, rails are joined by a resistance R. There is a uniform magnetic field $\\mathrm{B}$ normal to the plane of the rails, as shown in the figure. The terminal speed of the copper rod is:\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/nPtk98OV8m_xU2gG5kncRd0J3LvljrdeUJRyRI0A220.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "WNrm5",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{mgR} \\cos \\theta}{\\mathrm{B}^2 l^2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2BwXe",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{mgR} \\sin \\theta}{\\mathrm{B}^2 l^2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "YnPLZ",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{mgR} \\tan \\theta}{\\mathrm{B}^2 l^2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gmp5m",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{mgR} \\cot \\theta}{\\mathrm{B}^2 l^2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "From Faraday's law of electomagnetic induction,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ne &=\\frac{d \\phi}{d t}=\\frac{d(B A)}{l t}=\\frac{d(B l l)}{d t} \\\\\n&=\\frac{B d l \\times l}{d t}=B V l\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nAlso, $F=i l B=\\left(\\frac{B V}{R}\\right)\\left(l^2 B\\right)=\\frac{B^2 l^2 V}{R}$\nAt equilibrium\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/IThq93sgx3l5iFAgin_lVatWj22hs8CBE9bN-ro8ftM.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$$\nm g \\sin \\theta=\\frac{B^2 l V}{R} \\Rightarrow V=\\frac{m g R \\sin \\theta}{B^2 l^2}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
